### Normalized scores (1-100)

The following values are v4-normalized interpretations of verified capability evidence, not official benchmark scores. Different evaluation efforts and harnesses are identified above; missing benchmark results are not imputed.

\- Tool use: 84/100. Strong agentic evidence from Tau3 Banking, GDPval-AA, AutomationBench-AA, SWE Atlas QA and OSWorld 2.0. Performance is capped below frontier level by Tau3 Banking remaining below the 50% reference threshold, GDPval-AA remaining below 1,750 Elo, and the absence of an exact Terminal-Bench 2.1 result.

\- Reasoning: 90/100. GPQA Diamond exceeds the 90% frontier threshold and HLE exceeds the 40% threshold. AA-LCR and CritPt provide additional support. The Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index remains below the 60+ frontier anchor, preventing a higher normalized score.

\- Context window: 98/100. Official 1,050,000-token total context places it in the ≥1M tier. The score is capped below 100 because no verified ≥98% retrieval result at 512K or longer was found.

\- Multimodal: 80/100. Supports text, image and PDF inputs, with text output. The score follows the PDF-capable tier (75–90) but is capped by the lack of native audio/video support and non-text output. Supporting image-understanding evidence includes MMMU-Pro 86.0% (Artificial Analysis, max effort; rank 4/72).&#x20;

[image](https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=https://benchmarklist.com\&sz=32)

BenchmarkList



\- Coding: 92/100. DeepSWE 1.1 exceeds the 74% frontier anchor, while SciCode is above 55%. SWE Atlas QA, Vibe Code Bench, and the separate SWE-Marathon result support strong software-development capability. Missing SWE-bench Verified and Terminal-Bench 2.1 scores cap confidence in a still higher score.

\- Cost efficiency: 73/100. Evaluated on the standard paid OpenCode Zen/API tier at $2 input and $10 output per 1M tokens, with $0.10 cached input. This lies between the supplied approximate $1.25/$4.25 anchor (\~88) and $3/$15 anchor (\~60). Larger-context requests carry a pricing premium. Cost is scored independently.

\- Overall Score: 88.8/100. `(84 + 90 + 98 + 80 + 92) / 5 = 88.8`, half-up rounded to one decimal. Best fit: complex coding and debugging, long-context document analysis, computer-use agents and multi-step professional workflows where strong capability is required without flagship-tier token pricing. Cost efficiency is excluded from the overall mean.

